<title>GERMANY: German January-June metals output detailed.</title>
<headline>German January-June metals output detailed.</headline>
<dateline>ESCHBORN, Germany 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>German copper and lead output rose in the first half of 1997 while zinc and aluminium output was down on the same 1996 period, official figures showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>Base metals data from the state statistics office Bundesamt fuer Wirtschaft (BAW) also showed output of semi-finished non-ferrous metals products in the six months was higher than a year earlier.</p>
<p>The report gave the following details, in tonnes --</p>
<p>METALS OUTPUT	  June 97  Jan/June 97 Cumulative pct change</p>
<p>							     over Jan/June 96</p>
<p>primary aluminium	46,851  282,054		  -  2.0</p>
<p>electrolytic copper    50,477  298,628		  +  1.8</p>
<p>zinc			 27,550  159,101		  -  2.5</p>
<p>refined lead	     21,482  121,615		  + 34.8</p>
<p>SEMI-FINISHED MTLS   June 97  Jan/June 97 Pct change over 1996</p>
<p>aluminium		 161,482  880,049		  + 20.9</p>
<p>copper		    142,176  802,887		  + 12.7</p>
<p>zinc			 16,632   87,487		  + 10.3</p>
<p>lead			  4,678   24,909		  + 15.4</p>
<p>nickel			1,966   10,702		  + 19.7</p>
<p>METALS CASTINGS	June 97  Jan/June 97 Pct change over 1996</p>
<p>aluminium		  47,133  268,273		  +  7.9</p>
<p>copper			7,099   39,414		  +  8.4</p>
<p>zinc			  5,767   33,317		  +  3.6</p>
<p>lead			    284    2,527		  - 24.3</p>
<p>tin				22	109		  +  2.8</p>
<p>Semis and castings figures include alloys. Nickel castings data were not given.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
